agentd-instruction — third-party material included in this crate
================================================================

This crate's own source is AGPL-3.0-only (see the repository's LICENSE).
Two artifacts in it come from the Instruction Specification
(https://github.com/instruction-md/specification), owned by instruction.md,
and carry their own terms. They are named here because this notice ships
inside the published package: attribution has to travel with the copy, and a
crate that redistributes someone else's material without saying so is silent
in exactly the place a reader would look.

1. `src/instruction.schema.json`
   The specification's machine-readable registry — kinds, forms, grants and
   semantic rules — read as DATA by the parser, which is why the parser cannot
   drift from the specification.
   Licence: **CC BY 4.0**.
   Attribution: "The Instruction Specification", instruction.md,
   https://github.com/instruction-md/specification.

2. `tests/conformance/**`
   The specification's conformance corpus: the shared fixtures this
   implementation and the TypeScript one (`@instruction-md/spec`) are both
   held to.
   Licence: **Apache-2.0** — the full text is at
   `tests/conformance/LICENSE`, copied alongside the fixtures with the
   corpus README as that licence requires.

Both licences permit redistribution with attribution, which this notice and
the copied LICENSE provide. Neither artifact is compiled into the library as
code: the schema is parsed at runtime as data, the corpus is test input.
